criminal|PASS: The novel is fictional; lawbreaker and criminal-law adjective have separate POS and ordinals. The noun definition does not presume every suspect guilty. Vietnamese preserves stolen paintings and contract contrast; countability and attributive law construction are sound.
homework|PASS: Teacher-assigned tasks outside lessons define the uncountable schoolwork sense. Vietnamese keeps the history subject and before-meal sequence. Grammar explicitly rejects a homework without confusing the task with a physical sheet.
mouse|PASS: Rodent and pointing-device senses are distinct; cupboard movement and moving a photograph identify each clearly. Vietnamese names the device in the instruction. Animal mice versus device mice/mouses is qualified, with no rat or touchpad identity merge.
register|REVIEW: [SENSE_BOUNDARY] Enrolment and official-list noun accurately represent source ordinals 0 and 1; for/with/in constructions were checked against accessible Cambridge search text. That text also documents measurement and other noun uses absent from these two source boundaries. Additional scope needs editorial review; this is not an exhaustive register inventory.
seventy|PASS: The cardinal definition and seventy-chair example agree, with no digit mismatch. Seventieth is correctly marked ordinal; the supported NUMBER proposal remains scoped to continuation and does not approve a canonical taxonomy category.
